			Vendored (3rd party) code.
Licence information can be found in each subfolder of this directory.

Era-accurate LibWWW version pulled from here:
https://www.w3.org/History/1992/WWWLibrary_2.11.tar.Z
With a large part of the codebase stripped out such as build scripts and
irrelevant platform code. The archive suggests the archive is from 1992 but the
licence statement indicates 1993, it is used with the assumption that the 1992
date is correct and may be amended in future to use an older archive if
possible.

Python 0.9.1 from 1991 pulled from
https://www.python.org/ftp/python/src/Python-0.9.1.tar.gz.

GLM extracted from here:
https://ftp.zx.net.nz/pub/archive/ftp.sgi.com/sgi/opengl/CAL/s97demos.sgi.tar.gz
for a closer to era-accurate OBJ parser.

LibTIFF v3.4 beta 018 from
https://download.osgeo.org/libtiff/old/tiff-v3.4beta018-tar.gz
is from 1995 as tracking down a version from 1992 has not-yet proved fruitful.

XLib is going to be stuck requiring whatever very late system version is
available for now, as the original GLX was proprietary until 1999.

